& [SMBC-001_SourcePreservation]
  + raw dictation manifest canonical specification and executable artifacts remain separate identities
  + [support] source manifest SJS review SemanticCompilerFrontEnd source map and lifecycle

& [SMBC-002_MinimalSeed]
  + a seed binds external trust dependency discovery compiler capability and successor policy without private keys or self-approval
  + [support] SOPSeed SeedExpansion BootstrapKernel dependency

& [SMBC-003_SemanticFrontEnd]
  + canonical SOP resolves to typed backend-neutral IR with exact semantic addresses contracts dependencies unresolved accounts and capability ceilings
  + [support] SemanticCompilerFrontEnd and CandidateCompilationPlan

& [SMBC-004_AttentionBackend]
  + attention procedures bind focus inputs outputs transforms gates faculty checkpoints tools stops continuation and reentry while claiming no hidden-state access
  + [support] AttentionProcedureBackend and existing deterministic procedure-compiler precursor

& [SMBC-005_InferenceHostBackend]
  + external adapters precede internal llama.cpp extensions and internal work requires measured signed limitation evidence plus version ABI and rebase proof
  + [support] InferenceHostBackend

& [SMBC-006_NativeBackend]
  + conventional Rust C C++ service CLI library and later HDL candidates retain exact toolchain build artifact interface capability and rollback identity
  + [support] NativeArtifactBackend

& [SMBC-007_BackendSeparation]
  + no artifact capability receipt or admission profile transfers between attention host-integration and native targets
  + [support] BackendSeparation mutation acceptance and multi-plan rule

& [SMBC-008_SelfAssemblyStages]
  + self-description self-ordering self-hosting and self-revision are independently observable maturity states
  + [support] SelfAssemblyLedger and Speak Into Order dependency

& [SMBC-009_ExternalRecognition]
  + a candidate successor cannot replace its predecessor without independent Honesty Security verification and external authority recognition
  + [support] CompilationLifecycle SOPSeed successor policy and SelfAssemblyLedger

& [SMBC-010_Traceability]
  + source IR plan build artifact receipt signature admission installation generation and rollback deltas remain replayable
  + [support] source maps digests receipts and ledger

& [SMBC-011_PrototypeOrder]
  + inert semantic planning precedes sandboxed candidate production which precedes signed fixture admission
  + [support] implementation slices and prototype plan

& [SMBC-012_FacultyAccount]
  + all seven faculties have distinct duties across meaning capability planning projection refinement record and closure
  + [support] SJS faculty review and per-slice acceptance

& [Coverage]
  + [specification_gaps] none_for_declared_P0_architecture
  + [implementation_gaps] SMBC-001_through_SMBC-012
  + [first_dependency] Semantic Anchor Catalogue Slice4B2 proof-bearing lexical query
  + [first_legal_implementation] separately preserved and phase-locked pure form slice

